{"pageid": 942, "title": "Oscuratype", "revid": 2447, "categories": ["Lore", "Monsters", "Oscuratypes"], "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><figure class=\"thumb  show-info-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" style=\"width: 180px\"> \t<a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/0/05/Oscuratype.png/revision/latest?cb=20241215001149\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"Oscuratype\" src=\"data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"180\" height=\"284\" class=\"thumbimage lazyload\" data-image-name=\"Oscuratype.png\" data-image-key=\"Oscuratype.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" data-src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/0/05/Oscuratype.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241215001149\" /></a> \t<noscript><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/0/05/Oscuratype.png/revision/latest?cb=20241215001149\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"Oscuratype\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/0/05/Oscuratype.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241215001149\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"180\" height=\"284\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-image-name=\"Oscuratype.png\" data-image-key=\"Oscuratype.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" data-src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/0/05/Oscuratype.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241215001149\" /></a></noscript> \t<figcaption class=\"thumbcaption\"> \t\t \t\t\t<a href=\"/wiki/File:Oscuratype.png\" class=\"info-icon\"><svg><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-info-small\"></use></svg></a> \t\t \t\t \t\t \t</figcaption> </figure>\n<table align=\"center\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; border-style:none; background-color:transparent;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td width=\"20\" valign=\"top\" style=\"color:#7B68EE;font-size:40px;font-family:serif;font-weight:bold;text-align:left;padding:10px 10px;\">“\n</td>\n<td style=\"padding:4px 10px;\"><i>Fear needs to go somewhere. Fear needs to become something</i>\n</td>\n<td width=\"20\" valign=\"bottom\" style=\"color:#7B68EE;font-size:40px;font-family:serif;font-weight:bold;text-align:right;padding:10px 10px;\">”\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&#160;\n</td>\n<td valign=\"top\"><div style=\"line-height:1em;text-align: right\"><cite style=\"font-style:normal;\">&#8212; <i><a href=\"/wiki/Book_of_Butcher_1\" title=\"Book of Butcher 1\">Book of Butcher</a></i></cite></div><i></i>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><b>Oscuratypes</b> are a breed of <a href=\"/wiki/Monsters\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Monsters\">monster</a> fought by <a href=\"/wiki/The_Order_of_St._George\" title=\"The Order of St. George\">The Order of St. George</a>. Made from humanity's base, uncategorized fears, they are very populous and highly dangerous.\n</p>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"History\">History</span></h2>\n<table align=\"center\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; border-style:none; background-color:transparent;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td width=\"20\" valign=\"top\" style=\"color:#7B68EE;font-size:40px;font-family:serif;font-weight:bold;text-align:left;padding:10px 10px;\">“\n</td>\n<td style=\"padding:4px 10px;\"><i>It is a strange but fascinating scenario where Oscuratypes were the monsters we faced when we know nothing, and now they are the monsters we face when we know so much.</i>\n</td>\n<td width=\"20\" valign=\"bottom\" style=\"color:#7B68EE;font-size:40px;font-family:serif;font-weight:bold;text-align:right;padding:10px 10px;\">”\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&#160;\n</td>\n<td valign=\"top\"><div style=\"line-height:1em;text-align: right\"><cite style=\"font-style:normal;\">&#8212; <i><a href=\"/wiki/Book_of_Butcher_1\" title=\"Book of Butcher 1\">Book of Butcher</a></i></cite></div><i></i>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Many believe that the Oscuratypes were the original monsters. Unlike other monsters, which come from specific phobias, Oscuratypes come from \"vague, generalized fears and anxieties.\" While their numbers dwindled with the rise of civilization and specific folklore, their population surged once again with the advent of science and lack of belief in aforementioned stories. By the 21st century, the advent of the inernet and global communication rose Oscuratype populations to an all-time high.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-BOB&#95;1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-BOB-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\">Description</span></h2>\n<figure class=\"thumb  show-info-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" style=\"width: 180px\"> \t<a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/2/2e/OscuratypeBabiesVErica7.png/revision/latest?cb=20241215170507\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"A litter of Oscuratype babies, .\" src=\"data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"180\" height=\"80\" class=\"thumbimage lazyload\" data-image-name=\"OscuratypeBabiesVErica7.png\" data-image-key=\"OscuratypeBabiesVErica7.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" data-src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/2/2e/OscuratypeBabiesVErica7.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241215170507\" /></a> \t<noscript><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/2/2e/OscuratypeBabiesVErica7.png/revision/latest?cb=20241215170507\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"A litter of Oscuratype babies, .\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/2/2e/OscuratypeBabiesVErica7.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241215170507\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"180\" height=\"80\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-image-name=\"OscuratypeBabiesVErica7.png\" data-image-key=\"OscuratypeBabiesVErica7.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" data-src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/2/2e/OscuratypeBabiesVErica7.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241215170507\" /></a></noscript> \t<figcaption class=\"thumbcaption\"> \t\t \t\t\t<a href=\"/wiki/File:OscuratypeBabiesVErica7.png\" class=\"info-icon\"><svg><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-info-small\"></use></svg></a> \t\t \t\t \t\t \t\t\t<p class=\"caption\">A litter of Oscuratype babies, <i><a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_7\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children 7\">Something Is Killing the Children #7</a>.</i></p> \t\t \t</figcaption> </figure><p>Oscuratypes do not often have a physical form, and mainly manifest as creatures of shadow,<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-BOB&#95;1-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-BOB-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> with multiple, glowing eyes, a fanged mouth, and multiple clawed legs they can use to attack.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-SIKTC5&#95;2-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SIKTC5-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> These monsters only become solid when eating or attacking, which means that they are extremely difficult to kill without sacrifice.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-BOB&#95;1-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-BOB-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Unlike other monsters, the Oscuratype is also specifically able to live a life-cycle similar to those of non-monstrum. With the more meat they consume, they grow into larger and more adult forms, and thus can breed with each other and produce children. This method of repopulation makes them very dangerous and thus necessitates a quick discovery and killing. However, it also makes Oscuratypes favored for <a href=\"/wiki/The_Order_of_St._George\" title=\"The Order of St. George\">The Order of St. George</a>'s monster farms, as they are able to breed them, keep them weak, and bind them to <a href=\"/wiki/Totems\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Totems\">Totems</a>.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-BOB&#95;1-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-BOB-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notable_Oscuratypes\">Notable Oscuratypes</span></h2>\n<ul><li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Archer&#39;s Peak Oscuratype Mother (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQXJjaGVyJTI3c19QZWFrX09zY3VyYXR5cGVfTW90aGVyP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Archer's Peak Oscuratype Mother</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Archer&#39;s Peak Oscuratype Children (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQXJjaGVyJTI3c19QZWFrX09zY3VyYXR5cGVfQ2hpbGRyZW4/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">Archer's Peak Oscuratype Children</span></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Octo\" title=\"Octo\">Octo</a> <i>(now <a href=\"/wiki/Phantasmatype\" title=\"Phantasmatype\">Phantasmatype</a> totem)</i></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Oscuratype_Totems\">Oscuratype Totems</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/House_of_Slaughter\" title=\"House of Slaughter\">House of Slaughter</a>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Octo\" title=\"Octo\">Octo</a></li></ul></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Gallery\">Gallery</span></h2>\n<div id=\"gallery-0\" hash=\"0fbd8161c38d636aa1e8c87c1fe4fa2d\" data-seq-no=\"0\" class=\"wikia-gallery wikia-gallery-caption-below wikia-gallery-position-left wikia-gallery-spacing-medium wikia-gallery-border-small wikia-gallery-captions-left wikia-gallery-caption-size-medium\"><div class=\"wikia-gallery-caption\"></div><div class=\"w